          </h2>

          <p>
            The Bobby Approved smoothie costs about $2.55 per 25 g of protein at the $50.99 Amazon price we saw for a 20-serving bag, and $3.00 per 25 g at FlavCity's $59.99 list price. FlavCity's subscription brings its own price down to $50.99 as well, and a first-order discount cuts it further. Those figures count all 25 g of protein on the panel, including the collagen.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you count only the roughly 15 g of non-collagen protein per scoop, the math changes sharply: $50.99 buys 300 g of complete protein, or about $4.25 per 25 g. That is the number to compare if you are buying protein for muscle and recovery, and it is two to three times what a Costco whey costs. The smoothie makes more sense when you compare it with a café smoothie or a ready-to-drink shake, which it beats easily.
